From 8d6cc4de1d24234a2ba62bbc6e2457f8ca0ba8c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:09:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_create: a placed create the target rejected
 reports the refusal, never "IS created"

Review t_01a1cf610e4e2f39 on the previous commit: _place_remote never read a
terminal rejection. When await_task_id returned (None, None) because the
request was rejected/expired/failed, the creator chat was still told "The card
IS created ... Do NOT call kanban_create again" with task_id null. With the
new origin_idempotency_conflict refusal that turned a visible duplicate into
silently lost work.

Now a rejected request returns a tool error (created: false) carrying the
target's code. origin_idempotency_conflict names the card that holds the key
as existing_task_id (kanban_create's key semantics), with how to read it or
pick another key; any other refusal says no card was created and why. A still
pending request keeps the "IS created" note.
